  "description": "Sandgrouse — medium-sized, ground-dwelling birds of arid and semi-arid regions, placed in their own order. They are pigeon-like in shape but with pointed wings, a short bill, and feathered legs. Their most remarkable adaptation is the ability of males to absorb water in specially modified belly feathers and carry it to chicks at nests up to 30 km from the nearest water. Cryptic plumage renders them nearly invisible against desert gravel.",
